[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ML-L Software Requirements Specification
VERSION: 1.0.0
DATE: 2026-01-01

[SECTION]
TITLE: Functional Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Inference execution
STATEMENT: >>>
The ML-L shall execute inference on the configured input and produce a
result within the defined timeout.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-REQ-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Deterministic output
STATEMENT: >>>
The ML-L shall produce bit-identical output across repeated inferences on
the same input, given the same model and runtime configuration.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-REQ-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Inference latency
STATEMENT: >>>
The ML-L shall execute inference within the latency budget defined for the
target platform and workload type.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Memory footprint
STATEMENT: >>>
The ML-L runtime shall not exceed the peak resident memory limit defined
for the target platform during inference execution.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Analysis

[SECTION]
TITLE: Non-Functional Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-NFR-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ECSS compliance
STATEMENT: >>>
The ML-L shall be developed and qualified in accordance with
ECSS-E-ST-40C and ECSS-Q-ST-80C.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Review

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-NFR-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Code coverage
STATEMENT: >>>
Unit test coverage shall achieve a minimum of 80% line coverage and
75% function coverage across all ML-L source modules.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ML-L-NFR-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Static analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
The ML-L source code shall contain no CRITICAL-severity issues as reported
by the configured static analysis tool.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
